<title>USA: HCC Insurance Q4 shr $0.35 vs $0.24.</title>
<headline>HCC Insurance Q4 shr $0.35 vs $0.24.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>HCC INSURANCE HOLDINGS, INC.</p>
<p>				  Financial Highlights</p>
<p> Three Months Ended December 31,	     1996	   1995</p>
<p> Gross written premium		   $58,631,000  $74,075,000</p>
<p> Net written premium			27,837,000   24,396,000</p>
<p> Net earned premium			 27,212,000   21,160,000</p>
<p> Fee and commission income		 8,428,000    9,437,000</p>
<p> Net investment income		     4,219,000    3,658,000</p>
<p> Total revenue				41,424,000   35,000,000</p>
<p> Proforma net earnings (A)		12,564,000    8,921,000</p>
<p> Proforma earnings per share (A)		0.35	   0.25</p>
<p>Proforma operating earnings after tax (A)</p>
<p>						  11,456,000    8,416,000</p>
<p> Proforma operating earnings per share (A)  0.31	   0.24</p>
<p> Net earnings				 12,564,000    8,347,000</p>
<p> Earnings per share				 0.35	   0.24</p>
<p> Weighted average shares outstanding  36,387,000   35,156,000</p>
<p>NOTE: (A) Proforma adjustments have been made to the 1995 figures to reflect comparable compensation expense to LDG officers and to reflect appropriate income tax expense despite LDG's S Corporation (non-taxable) status prior to its reorganization and merger with the company.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
